{
  "comment": [
    "What a GraalVM native image cannot work out for itself: the signature of every",
    "downcall this library makes through the foreign linker. One that is missing builds",
    "cleanly and fails with MissingForeignRegistrationError where it is first called.",
    "The first image (22.09.2026) needed only mlock/munlock - jint (void*, jlong) - because",
    "that was all it reached; the TLS stack's P-256 through OpenSSL then failed in an image",
    "on 24.09.2026. So the list is now every signature in the source - OpenSSL and libc on",
    "Linux, bcrypt, ncrypt, crypt32, advapi32 and kernel32 on Windows - and",
    "NativeDowncallMetadataTest holds it to the source in both directions.",
    "Nothing else is needed. The drivers are found through ServiceLoader, which an image",
    "handles without help, and there is no reflection anywhere in the distribution -",
    "see NoReflectionTest, which keeps it that way."
  ],
